  "query_preview": "through Monday. High Surf Advisories will likely be needed \nbeginning late Saturday, continuing into early next week. Overall, \nconditions will be hazardous and dangerous and entering the surf is \nSTRONGLY discouraged. Even visiting the beach could become \nhazardous, especially during periods of high tide. \n\nWednesday-Thursday..At least a breezy NE flow looks to persist \nthrough middle of next week. There remains some differences in the \nmodels with how strong the pressure gradient remains between ridge \nto the north and lingering low pressure either well south or \nsoutheast of the area. This will continue hazardous surf and boating \nconditions, with lingering beach erosion and coastal flooding issues \nlikely. Isolated to scattered onshore moving showers remain in the\nforecast and temperatures will remain near around normal for this\ntime of year.",
